Package: simCoDaR
Title: Simulation of Compositional Data and Ideal Mineral Assays
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Matt", "Clauson", email = "matthewclauson@outlook.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates closed mineral compositions from hypothetical domain
    targets and fits multivariate distributions to measured assay
    subcompositions, including Dirichlet, logistic-normal, isometric log-ratio
    Student-t and Gaussian mixture models. Provides reproducible synthetic
    draws and held-out distributional diagnostics. Converts ideal fixed-formula
    mineral mass fractions to theoretical elemental and oxide reporting
    features with explicit units and mass-balance audits. Statistical assay
    fits do not establish physical mineral calibration, instrument response,
    spatial continuity or causal relationships.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: stats, withr
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown,
    ggplot2, ggdist, dplyr, tidyr, purrr, tibble
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
NeedsCompilation: no
